  - metadata-protocol `protocol.runtime-authoring-gate.test.ts`: 162/162.
  - Only objectql's result changes in round 2, so the rest of the sweep was not re-run (the seat's instruction).
- **Round 1 consumer sweep, at the `a0c24ab647` tree.** It covered every package whose tests save or publish through the gate (`git grep -l "publishPackageDrafts\|saveMetaItem" -- "packages/**/*.test.ts"`). Each ran `pnpm --filter PKG test --maxWorkers=2` under `os-verify-lock.sh`:
  - `@objectstack/lint` 148 files / 6934 tests passed;
  - `@objectstack/metadata-protocol` 248 passed, 3 skipped / 20733 passed, 19 skipped;
  - `@objectstack/objectql` 445 passed, 2 failed / 8407 passed, 7 failed. 6 were `protocol-duplicate-package-names-in-step.test.ts` (re-trued, 6/6) and 1 was the `duplicatePackage` case re-pinned in round 2;
  - `@objectstack/rest` 300 / 6095 passed; `@objectstack/runtime` 423 / 6655 passed; `@objectstack/core` 106 / 2580; `@objectstack/metadata` 63 / 892; `@objectstack/platform-objects` 78 / 1188; `@objectstack/plugin-security` 188 / 3754; `@objectstack/service-automation` 192 / 2567; `@objectstack/service-cluster` 7 / 105; `@objectstack/service-datasource` 45 / 838; `@objectstack/cli` (both projects) 474 passed, 1 skipped / 6018 passed;
  - `@objectstack/dogfood`: the 7 files the grep names plus the re-trued `view-container-cross-package-default.dogfood.test.ts`, 8 files / 51 tests passed. The rest of the dogfood suite was not run locally (main's full battery runs it). A `git grep` for package-scoped view writes (`meta/view…?package=`) in `packages/qa/dogfood/test` names only the re-trued file;
  - `@objectstack/spec` was not run: it has no workspace dependency (`pg-connection-string`, `zod`), so no spec test can reach `@objectstack/lint`, and its grep hits are prose.
- Typechecks (round 1): `lint` (with `check:test-typecheck`), `metadata-protocol`, `objectql` and `dogfood` exit 0.
- **Ablation** (round 1, the seat's ask): the severity was set back to `warning`. `severity: 'error'` became `severity: String(object) === 'ablated_24563_warning' ? 'error' : 'warning'` through `scripts/ablation-replace.mjs` (anchor 1 → 0, blob `f38af8f08988` → `377fdb85d3dd`). Lint was rebuilt, and the marker was in 4 built files.
  - Lint file: 4 red, 23 green. The reds were the three refusal cases and the object-door refusal in the flow case. The CLI case checks the rule id only and stayed green.
  - Protocol block: 5 red ((a) ×2, (d), (e), (g)) and 5 green (the draft save, (b) ×2, (c), (f)). Exactly the refusal legs went red, and every control held.
  - Restore: blob == HEAD, `git diff HEAD` empty, rebuild, `--absent` from all 20 built files, tree clean. The lint file passed 27/27 and the protocol file 162/162.
  - The lint source (blob `f38af8f08988`) is unchanged in `483b3ec995`.

### Round 0

- Pre-merge head `cab356c0ce` (the same code as `fe5bafb2be`, which added only the changeset and the docs sentence):
  - `pnpm --filter @objectstack/metadata-protocol exec vitest run --maxWorkers=2`: 248 files passed (3 skipped), 20731 tests passed (19 skipped). `typecheck` passed.
